## Lore

Swordsmanship has been an art among the Amaki since clan disputes were
settled by duels at dawn, and the Duelists are its masters: master psychics
who pour their power into the blade. Raised from childhood in the House of the
Sword, they learn first to handle any sword perfectly and then to call up a
blade of pure psychic force, with only a few other powers kept to guard body
and mind.

The House of the Sword also teaches fencing to the rest of Amaki society, and
the rumour that it hires out its members as spies and assassins is true.
Duelists are trained as soldiers and secret agents too, and on covert work they
leave the psi-blade behind and carry an ordinary blast-sword. They are the most
serious of the Amaki, with little of their people''s love of pleasure, and
often travel alone on missions for their House.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'duelist');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'duelist';

